[P1] Self-monitoring of an isolated power station
[P2] On a hard-to-reach plateau, one station feeds a dispensary, a radio relay, weather instruments and safety lighting. The micro-grid is made up of solar panels, lithium batteries and a small diesel generator. Since the road can remain closed for days, a controller measures the voltage, the current. temperature and vibration every 200 milliseconds. Detailed data remains in place, only a compressed summary is transmitted when the link is operational. Medical equipment and communications are a priority.
[P3] On October 18, 2025, a dust storm reduced solar output by 34% in fifteen minutes. The temperature of the battery compartment rose by 8°C, while the inverter fan produced an abnormal vibration. Instead of shutting down the station, the system turned off the secondary heating, reduced some of the lights, and started the rescue team. He identified three possible causes of debris on the panels, a worn-out bearing and increasing resistance in a battery connector.
[P4] After the storm, a head-mounted camera read the license plates and alarm codes, then a local processor compared them to the offline manual No sensitive images were sent to the cloud The software required the entire tag to remain within a certain margin, it also controlled the overall sharpness and that of the top part A voice command asked to back off if an edge was missing, and four stable frames were needed. The engineers then confirmed the proposed order: clean the panels, replace the bearing, and then tighten the connector. The intervention lasted six minutes without interrupting a critical service A reliable automation must recognize uncertainty and leave the final decision to the operator
============================================================

